# Each unit reads its own `.env` at $AVA_HOME/.env (a single box uses ~/.ava).
# `scripts/install.sh` sets up the host; copy this file to $AVA_HOME/.env and fill
# it in. Required fields first, then the capability keys (fill these or the
# matching feature is unavailable), then truly-optional extras.
#
# Note: do not put `COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME` here — the docker compose project name is
# always `ava` (the shared infra project), set by `cli/commands/_compose.py:_compose_project_name`.

# --- required ---------------------------------------------------------------
# This host's capability set: two independent booleans. `gateway` owns the data
# plane + HTTP gateway; `agent-runner` runs agents. A single box sets both true;
# split deployments give each its own machine. Unset -> falls back to the
# $AVA_HOME/machine_serve_* file; if neither resolves true, `ava start` fails. On
# an agent-runner `ava enroll` writes these for you.
AVA_MACHINE_SERVE_GATEWAY=true
AVA_MACHINE_SERVE_AGENT_RUNNER=true
# Stable identifier for this host (memory branch / machines-table key).
AVA_MACHINE_NAME=
# A host with `gateway` points at its own pg/redis. A runner-only host points at
# the gateway's reachable pg/redis endpoint (it has no local data plane).
# pg loopback is trust (the password is ignored on 127.0.0.1). With a bearer
# set, Postgres uses the gateway-only DB-admin password; Redis `requirepass`
# uses the gateway-only Redis-admin password; its runtime URL embeds the
# independent Redis ACL password. An EMPTY AVA_CLUSTER_SECRET is the single-box
# no-auth posture: gateway API / /ops / pg / redis all serve unauthenticated on
# loopback. An install derives these URLs — edit them only for a dev-only
# stand-in like below.
#
# AVA_DB_URL is the ONE database access URL every process dials as-is. Its port
# is chosen at install/converge by AVA_PGBOUNCER_ENABLED: the cluster's
# PgBouncer listener (the default home's 6433) when pooling is on (the default),
# the direct Postgres port (5433) when off — a normal process never needs to
# know the pooler exists. Only the gateway's admin plane (migrations / pg_dump)
# uses the direct URL, derived from the registry record. Flipping
# AVA_PGBOUNCER_ENABLED=false is the kill-switch: converge rewrites this URL to
# the direct port and the pooler never starts.
# Illustrative only — the install writes the real per-cluster URLs under
# $AVA_HOME (default ports: Postgres 5433, Redis 6380). Do not copy these
# over the generated .env.
AVA_DB_URL=postgresql://ava:ava_dev_only@localhost:5433/ava
AVA_REDIS_URL=redis://ava:ava_dev_only@localhost:6380/0
# Optional unit-local executable directory; both redis-server and redis-cli
# must exist and be executable. Absolute path only; empty keeps brew/PATH.
# Use `ava config set --local redis_bin_dir=/absolute/redis/bin` to persist it.
# AVA_REDIS_BIN_DIR=
# Connection-layer knobs for a swappable data plane (Task #1752). The URLs are
# the switch: pointing AVA_DB_URL / AVA_REDIS_URL at another host (a remote
# machine on the private network, or a SaaS provider) makes this cluster treat
# the data plane as remote-managed — local instance bring-up / stop / ACL /
# pooler provisioning are skipped and degrade to reachability probes. TLS,
# pool sizing, and identity ride the URLs or these fields:
# - TLS: PostgreSQL sslmode (empty = URL / libpq default 'prefer'; a SaaS URL
#   that already carries sslmode wins). Redis TLS rides the URL scheme
#   (rediss://) and its query params. Identity / ACL mapping rides the URL
#   userinfo (names-as-data — the provider's user IS the role).
# AVA_DB_SSLMODE=
# - Pool sizing defaults for shared.db.pool() (explicit per-caller sizes win).
# AVA_DB_POOL_MIN_SIZE=
# AVA_DB_POOL_MAX_SIZE=
# Gateway-home only: install mints these independently for an authenticated
# cluster. Never put these standalone keys on an agent-runner; bootstrap carries
# only its least-privilege DB/Redis URLs.
# AVA_DB_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# AVA_REDIS_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# AVA_RUNNER_DB_PASSWORD=
# AVA_REDIS_PASSWORD=
# Route runtime DB connections through this cluster's PgBouncer transaction
# pooler (ON by default — the density path past ~50 agents). Set false as a
# kill-switch (+ restart) to fall back to direct Postgres; the port AVA_DB_URL
# carries follows this toggle. Only meaningful on a gateway-capable host.
# AVA_PGBOUNCER_ENABLED=false
# Host the per-cluster data-plane URLs are DERIVED with (install birth). Empty
# = loopback (127.0.0.1) — the single-box posture. Set it to a reachable
# address when the data plane is hosted off-box (external-migration step of
# Task #1752); the born AVA_DB_URL / AVA_REDIS_URL then carry that host and
# every dial follows the URL. Read at birth only (the registry record carries
# the snapshot); existing clusters keep their URLs until re-derived.
# AVA_DATA_PLANE_HOST=
# Pick a model; its provider key below must be set. claude-* uses ANTHROPIC_API_KEY,
# deepseek-* uses DEEPSEEK_API_KEY (DeepSeek's anthropic-compatible endpoint),
# gpt-* uses OPENAI_API_KEY.
AVA_MODEL=deepseek-v4-pro
# Model for the short conversation-name labeler only (one call per agent).
# Prompts here are often machine-authored agent briefs, which a weaker model
# executes instead of summarizing (issue #178); uncomment to override.
# AVA_LABELER_MODEL=deepseek-v4-pro
# On the gateway: set to this host's own public URL (used to build user-facing links).
# On an agent-runner: set to the gateway's public URL it reaches over the network.
# Clients resolve the HTTP base via shared.machine.gateway_api_base() — localhost on the gateway.
AVA_GATEWAY_URL=
# The single per-cluster pre-shared control-plane bearer. It authenticates
# gateway API, /ops, bootstrap, and machine registration; it is never a
# Postgres, PgBouncer, or Redis password. A URL-safe token (letters / digits /
# - . _ ~) — change it from this dev placeholder. Hand it to each split runner
# via `ava enroll`.
# Single-box installs leave it EMPTY on purpose (no-auth loopback; see the
# AVA_DB_URL comment). Split deployments require it on every host — `ava start`
# fails fast without it there.
AVA_CLUSTER_SECRET=ava_dev_only

# --- capability keys (fill these — each gates a built-in feature) ------------
# Model provider keys: set the one(s) your AVA_MODEL (and any per-agent override)
# needs. build_chat_model fails fast on a missing key.
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-...
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# Gemini — `ava.understand`'s media path (image/video/audio/PDF). The default
# media model is gemini-3.5-flash, so without this any media understand call raises.
# Keys start with `AIza`.
GEMINI_API_KEY=AIza...
# The Gemini endpoint the media path dials is configurable (commented default;
# a self-hosted relay or provider mirror can be pointed at without code
# changes). It receives the same auth as Gemini (GEMINI_API_KEY). The media
# path currently supports Gemini models only (the media wire format is
# Gemini-specific); a non-Gemini model id fails fast with a clear error.
# AVA_UNDERSTAND_MEDIA_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com
# Brave Search — backs `ava.web.search`. Without it, web search raises.
# Keys start with `BSA`. The endpoint is configurable (commented default:
# a self-hosted relay or provider mirror can be pointed at without code
# changes); a custom endpoint must accept `X-Subscription-Token` with the key.
# AVA_WEB_BRAVE_SEARCH_ENDPOINT=https://api.search.brave.com/res/v1/web/search
BRAVE_API_KEY=BSA...
# Jina Reader — backs `ava.web.fetch`. Optional but recommended: empty = anonymous
# tier (20 RPM); with a key = 500 RPM. The reader base is configurable
# (commented default; a self-hosted mirror can be pointed at without code
# changes); it must end with `/` and accept `Authorization: Bearer` with the key.
# AVA_WEB_JINA_BASE_URL=https://r.jina.ai/
JINA_API_KEY=jina_...
# Zhipu GLM — backs glm-* models (e.g. glm-5.2). OpenAI-compatible endpoint
# at https://open.bigmodel.cn/api/paas/v4. Empty = glm-* models unavailable.
GLM_API_KEY=...
# Xiaomi MiMo — backs mimo-* models. OpenAI-compatible endpoint at
# https://api.xiaomimimo.com/v1. Empty = mimo-* models unavailable.
MIMO_API_KEY=...
# Moonshot Kimi — backs kimi-* models. Empty = kimi-* models unavailable.
MOONSHOT_API_KEY=sk-...
# xAI Grok — backs grok-* models. Empty = grok-* models unavailable.
# Keys start with `xai-`.
XAI_API_KEY=xai-...
# Alibaba Cloud Model Studio (DashScope) — backs qwen* models (qwen3.8-max,
# qwen3.8-27b). Empty = qwen* models unavailable.
DASHSCOPE_API_KEY=...
# The OpenAI-compatible endpoint those models dial. The default is Alibaba's
# public Beijing host; a DEDICATED Model Studio workspace serves the same API on
# its own host and the default cannot reach it, so set this for such accounts:
#   https://<workspace-id>.cn-beijing.maas.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1
# Keep the /compatible-mode/v1 suffix (/api/v1 is the native protocol). Other
# regions price differently — see shared/lm/pricing_catalog.json.
# AVA_DASHSCOPE_BASE_URL=https://dashscope.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1

# --- optional ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Telegram push channel (ui.telegram) — agent -> owner's phone, one direction.
# - empty token = `python -m ui.telegram` does not start
# - owner_id = your Telegram user_id (the number, not the @username); the sole
#   push target. Get it from @userinfobot, or message the bot once and read
#   update.message.from.id from getUpdates.
#   0 (default) = no target, every push is dropped (guards against token leaks).
# Use: agent calls `ava.channels.telegram.send(text)` to push to your phone
# (often with ava.watcher.cron, e.g. "remind me to journal at 9am every day").
# owner_id must be a valid int even when telegram is off — leave it 0, do NOT
# blank it out (a present-but-empty `AVA_TELEGRAM_OWNER_ID=` fails int parsing
# and aborts settings load on a fresh `cp .env.example`).
AVA_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
AVA_TELEGRAM_OWNER_ID=0

# Split-deployment converge preflights. On by default, auto-skipped on a single box.
# Cross-machine transfer backend is probed, never required: `drive` warns (does not
# block) when no writable Google Drive synced folder is found; `none` skips the
# probe on a split agent-runner that moves files its own way.
# AVA_CROSS_MACHINE_TRANSFER_BACKEND=none
# Set false on a split agent-runner that does not consolidate the memory pool via
# GitHub PRs, so `ava start` does not require that to be wired up.
# AVA_REQUIRE_GITHUB_PR=false

# Multi-host (split deployment). The default is multi-machine; a single box is just
# the case where the reachable address is loopback. AVA_MACHINE_HOST defaults to
# localhost, so a single box is zero-config and binds loopback only. For a split
# deployment set it to this node's real private-network address — pg/redis then bind
# loopback + that address (de-duplicated, never all interfaces). Remote connections
# authenticate with their role-specific data-plane credentials over
# AVA_TRUSTED_CIDRS. Every node carries AVA_CLUSTER_SECRET for gateway control
# calls; `ava enroll` presents it to the gateway's authenticated /api/bootstrap.
# AVA_MACHINE_HOST=100.x.y.z
# AVA_TRUSTED_CIDRS=100.64.0.0/10

# WARNING: do not set this in dev .env! Only for e2e tests / advanced debugging
# scenarios (tests/e2e/README.md) — this routes all agent processes' LLM through
# the specified fake factory and never hits the real API.
# When set, agent startup will logger.warning loudly to remind you.
# AVA_LLM_OVERRIDE=tests.e2e.fakes.scenarios.<name>:build

# Local trace recording (OTel spans -> $AVA_HOME/traces/ JSONL mirror).
# Metadata-only by default: LLM content attributes are stripped at the source
# (TRACELOOP_TRACE_CONTENT=false) and again in the exporter, so the mirror stays
# ~KB/turn instead of the 31 GB/h full-content firehose (2026-08-05 incident).
# AVA_TRACE_ENABLED=true (default) to record, false to skip span recording.
# AVA_TRACE_STRIP_CONTENT=true (default) strips gen_ai.task.input/output,
# traceloop.entity.input/output, messages, system_instructions, etc.
# AVA_TRACE_RETENTION_DAYS=3 prunes day-stamped mirror files older than N days.
# AVA_TRACE_MAX_DIR_MB=2048 hard-caps the mirror directory (oldest files first).
# AVA_TRACE_DISK_WATERMARK=0.9 auto-disables recording when the data disk is
# over this usage fraction (1.0 or above disables the guard).

# OTLP dual-write (events -> Loki logs / Prometheus metrics) + the trace-ship
# target: `ava trace ship` replays the local mirror to Tempo over OTLP/HTTP at
# AVA_TELEMETRY_OTLP_ENDPOINT/v1/traces (the LGTM stack).
# AVA_TELEMETRY_OTLP_ENABLED=true (default) turns the whole OTLP surface on.
AVA_TELEMETRY_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:4318
